# Source-derived semantics

- The source contains one instruction paragraph followed by one empty 200px by 200px div.
- The tested declaration is background: bottom green scroll repeat-x; and is preserved verbatim.
- Without an image, the required green fill proves whether the complete valid shorthand parsed; inert position, attachment, and repeat tokens are intentionally retained.

# Compatibility adjustments

- Visible text uses one wrapping outer text with nested bold text and ordinary U+0020; the test box uses a class-scoped view.
- Content-box sizing and explicit body/paragraph spacing reproduce Web setup without relying on Lynx margin collapse.
- No tested background component is split, removed, or replaced.

# Current Lynx API-doc basis

- Background attachment is unsupported, so a future stable missing green fill would be an engine failure rather than grounds to rewrite or skip the assertion.
